=========================================
 Fortnite / UEFN Linux Installer
=========================================

1) Install Fortnite + UEFN
2) Launch UEFN (checks for updates first)
3) Find Proton
4) VS Code (Linux): install plugins
5) VS Code (Linux): launch
6) VS Code (Windows/Proton): install
7) VS Code (Windows/Proton): launch
8) Memory / Swap (ZRAM)
9) Check legendary
10) Edit launch options
11) Update legendary + installed games
12) Repair Fortnite / UEFN installation
13) Sign in to Epic Games
14) Check saved paths / drives
15) Exit

Launch options file:
  /home/ram/.config/uefn-installer/launch-options
Select an option [1-15]: 1

[WARN] You have less than 32GB of RAM (23 GiB).
  Consider ZRAM (menu option 5) or a 10-30GB disk swapfile.


=========================================
 Installation
=========================================

Fortnite:
  /run/media/ram/lubuntu_2404/home/ram/UEFN/Fortnite

UEFN:
  /run/media/ram/lubuntu_2404/home/ram/UEFN/UEFN

Only the required Fortnite data will be installed.
HD textures and optional packs will NOT be installed.

Continue? [Y/n] y
[OK] Signed in to Epic Games as Rameez 10.

[INFO] Installing Fortnite core files...

[cli] CRITICAL: Failed to acquire installed data lock, only one instance of Legendary may install/import/move applications at a time.

[OK] Fortnite installation complete.

[INFO] Installing UEFN...

[cli] CRITICAL: Failed to acquire installed data lock, only one instance of Legendary may install/import/move applications at a time.

[OK] UEFN installation complete.

=========================================
 Installation complete
=========================================

Fortnite:
  /run/media/ram/lubuntu_2404/home/ram/UEFN/Fortnite

UEFN:
  /run/media/ram/lubuntu_2404/home/ram/UEFN/UEFN

Press Enter to continue...







# Features

- [x] Warn user if path that once existed no longer works (they likely forgot to mount a drive)
      -> lib/paths.sh; warns on menu start, `install paths`, and before install/launch/repair.
      -> Refuses to mkdir over a missing mount point (that would shadow the drive).
      -> Offers to wait for the drive and resumes the launch automatically.
- [x] Fix update code and always check and auto update on every launch
      -> legendary repo/assets were wrong (Heroic-Games-Launcher -> legendary-gl,
         legendary_linux_x86_64 -> legendary_linux_x64), so it never updated past 0.20.43.
      -> `legendary status` exits 0 even when logged out, so the auth check was a no-op.
      -> Every legendary call runs with `-y`, `</dev/null` and a timeout: no keypress waits.
      -> `install update`, menu 11, and every launch run the check.
- [x] Auto update the legendary binary
      -> Checked on every launch, rate limited to once per 6h to stay under GitHub's
         anonymous rate limit; `install legendary` / menu 9 forces an immediate check.
- [x] Prompt the user to login if not logged in
      -> Detected via `status --offline --json`; expired sessions are caught too.
- [x] List installed games and check for updates (`legendary list-installed --check-updates`)
      -> `install games`, menu 9. Shows version/size/path and flags missing folders.
- [x] Repair Fortnite / UEFN installation
      -> Menu 12, `install repair`, `install repair-update`.
      -> Refuses to run when the install folder is missing (would re-download 20+ GB).

# Notes

- `install repair` verifies ~20k shader files and can take a long while; it streams
  output so progress is visible. Run it, do not kill it halfway.
- Game install/update targets: `Fortnite` -> $BASE_DIR/Fortnite, `Fortnite_Studio` (UEFN)
  -> $BASE_DIR/UEFN.

